1. GRANT (with valid license key)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Subject to the Subscriber's compliance with this License and, where an
updates-and-support term is in effect, continued payment of the
applicable license fee, the Author grants the Subscriber a
non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

  (a) install and use the Software on developer workstations and in the
      Subscriber's development, staging, and production deployments;
  (b) modify the Software for the Subscriber's internal use, provided
      that all copyright notices and license terms are preserved;
  (c) distribute the Software bundled inside the Subscriber's own
      application, provided the Software is not the primary product
      distributed, that it remains under this License, and that the
      distribution is not one of the cases in Section 1A.

License scope is set by the Subscriber's order:

  - Grid Developer License: the Software excluding the Spreadsheet
    Module and the Studio, on unlimited deployed production
    applications within the Subscriber's organization, plus unlimited
    internal dev / staging environments.
  - Suite Developer License: the Software in full, including the
    Spreadsheet Module and the Studio, on the same unlimited scope.
  - Enterprise / Custom (Site or Org-wide): scope per the negotiated
    order or master agreement.
  - OEM License: the redistribution cases in Section 1A.

The "Spreadsheet Module" is the workbook, formula engine and
spreadsheet file-format features: <SvSheet>, the <sv-sheet> element,
the formula evaluator, and the .xlsx / .xls / .ods / .csv readers and
writers. The "Studio" is the designer, the code generator and the SQL
data sources.

Using the Spreadsheet Module or the Studio under a Grid Developer
License is outside the licensed scope. The Software does not block it:
it stays soft-gated and shows the unlicensed watermark and notice until
the license is upgraded to Suite.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
1A. OEM AND REDISTRIBUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Section 1(c) covers the ordinary case, in which the Subscriber ships
its own application and the Software is one component inside it. An OEM
License, negotiated separately with the Author, is required where:

  (a) the Subscriber distributes the Software, or any part of it, to
      third parties as a component, library, SDK, template, or building
      block those third parties use to build their own applications;
  (b) the Subscriber's product is a platform, application builder,
      low-code or no-code tool, or development environment in which the
      Subscriber's own customers author applications, reports, or
      workbooks that render through the Software;
  (c) the Subscriber sublicenses, resells, or white-labels the Software
      under another name;
  (d) the Subscriber deploys the Software in a multi-tenant hosted
      product in which the Spreadsheet Module or the Studio is a
      material part of what the Subscriber's customers pay for.

An OEM License is priced separately from developer seats, is granted
for a defined term and a defined product, and may carry a
redistribution volume or royalty basis recorded in the order. Developer
seats do not convey these rights, however many are purchased.

For the avoidance of doubt, ordinary business software sold to
customers is covered by Section 1(c). A SaaS application whose users
view, edit and export their own data in a grid or a workbook is the
Subscriber's own application, not redistribution. The test is whether
third parties receive the Software as something they build with, not
whether the Subscriber charges for its product.

Requests: sales@jqwidgets.com.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. SEATS
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Software is licensed per developer. The number of seats and the
edition, Grid or Suite, are set by the Subscriber's order. All seats on
one order share one edition. A "developer" is any individual who writes or
modifies source code that imports `@svgrid/enterprise`. Read-only users
and end users do not count toward seats and are unlimited. One license
key activates every grid instance in scope; there is no per-page or
per-component accounting. A seat is tied to a role: if a developer
leaves and is replaced, the seat transfers to the replacement at no
additional cost.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. PERPETUAL LICENSE AND UPDATES/SUPPORT TERM
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The license is perpetual: the Subscriber may use the versions released
during a paid term forever. Each order includes one (1) year of updates
and support, which renews automatically each year at the then-current
rate until cancelled. The Subscriber may cancel at any time. On
cancellation or lapse:

  (a) every version released during a paid term keeps working and keeps
      validating against the Subscriber's license key;
  (b) the Subscriber stops receiving releases and support issued after
      the paid term ends.

The Author will not disable working features of a paying or previously
paying Subscriber.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. EVALUATION, SOFT-GATE, AND OPEN SOURCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Software is soft-gated. Every feature is fully functional without a
license key for evaluation. While unlicensed, the grid shows a small
"Unlicensed @svgrid/enterprise" watermark and emits a one-time console
notice; setting a valid key removes both. There is no time limit and no
disabled functionality during evaluation. Time-limited evaluation keys
that remove the watermark are available on request.

Projects that are open source under an OSI-approved license, hosted in a
public repository, and not a paid product qualify for a free Enterprise
key with the full feature set and no watermark, renewable annually.

License key validation is performed entirely client-side, signed against
the Author's public key. No network call is made to validate, and no
telemetry is sent. Air-gapped deployments are supported.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. RESTRICTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Subscriber may NOT:

  (a) redistribute the Software as a standalone package, library, or
      component;
  (b) sublicense, rent, lease, or sell the Software to third parties;
  (c) remove, obscure, or disable the license-key check or any
      copyright or proprietary notices;
  (d) use the Software to develop a data-grid, table, or spreadsheet
      component product that competes with the Software for
      distribution to third parties;
  (e) share license keys outside of the developer seats covered by the
      Subscriber's order;
  (f) ship to production a use of the Spreadsheet Module or the Studio
      that the Subscriber's edition does not cover, or a
      redistribution described in Section 1A without an OEM License.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. TERMINATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

On material breach of Sections 1, 1A, 2, or 5, the license terminates
automatically and the Subscriber must cease all use of the Software,
remove it from development environments, and stop deploying new versions
of any application that depends on it. Existing deployed copies in
production may continue to operate, but no new deployments are permitted.
Fees for licenses cancelled due to violation are non-refundable.

